<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gauls</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gallic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gauls</a> were Celtic peoples of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, living in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Gallic warriors served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> and allies in Carthaginian armies, notably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>'s campaign in Italy, and are mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a> profile.</p></div>
